claude-wg-client (Debian 12 WSL2)
================================

This is the CLIENT package; the Debian 12 VPS uses the separate server-side
claude-wg-peer package. Do not install the server package in this WSL instance.

Installing this package does not generate a key, modify /etc/resolv.conf, or
start the network. The target WSL instance must be bootstrapped under the
Windows-wide networkingMode=none setting. Only then, as root, run:

    claude-wg-client init-client --yes
    claude-wg-client check-files
    claude-wg-client arm-offline --yes
    claude-wg-client check-guard

The private key remains in this WSL instance at /etc/wireguard/claude.key.
Never export it to Windows, a package archive, Git or chat. Before first use,
run guest/configure-endpoint.sh so the packaged endpoint and peer public key
match your own server; arming offline does not establish an authenticated
tunnel until the VPS side has registered this client's public key.

The guard and tunnel are explicitly enabled for future starts only after the
guard passes checks. Windows WSL Hyper-V firewall, DNS-tunneling/autoProxy/
localhostForwarding settings and WSL startup ordering must be verified before
switching global WSL networking back to NAT. All WSL distributions share the
network namespace. A Windows/WSL administrator can bypass these protections.

Removal under NAT is refused while either service is active. Never stop the
guard to obtain direct Internet access. Package removal and purge preserve the
root-owned key, configuration and resolver; no automatic fallback is provided.
